    <statement><p>Decide, without calculation, if each of the integrals
below are positive, negative, or zero.  Let D be the 
region inside the unit circle centered at the origin.
Let T, B, R, and L denote the regions enclosed by the 
top half, the bottom half, the right half, and the 
left half of unit circle, respectively.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_B (y^3 + y^5) \, dA</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_T (y^3 + y^5) \, dA</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_D (y^3 + y^5) \, dA</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_L (y^3 + y^5) \, dA</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_R (y^3 + y^5) \, dA</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
